# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: Folio, from its release zip Folio-<ver>.zip.
Package: Folio
Section: Document
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Recommends: FolioCJK
Suggests: FolioSpeech, FolioOCR
Components: Apps.Document.!Folio (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-folio
Description: Reader for PDF and ebook files, built on MuPDF
 Folio reads PDF, EPUB, FB2, MOBI, CBZ and XPS files on the desktop:
 a bookshelf with covers, contents, find, two pages side by side, dark
 and sepia pages, text selection and copying, dictionary look-ups,
 PDF highlights and notes, forms, passwords, printing and export of a
 page as a Draw file.
 .
 Reading aloud (FolioSpeech), text recognition for scanned pages
 (FolioOCR) and fonts for Chinese, Japanese and Korean (FolioCJK) are
 separate packages.
Build-Map: !Folio -> Apps/Document/!Folio
Build-Notice: Folio, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-folio/releases
 .
